If the player dies at the same time as one of the bosses, they will be sent out of the fight arena as normal with one health point and the fight will be considered a victory.

===Eyatlalli's glyph===
[[File:Eyatlalli's glyph.png|thumb|250px|Eyatlalli's glyph, indicating a safe place to stand.]]
Surrounding the Moon are eight sigils that represent the moon's cycles; the waxing/waning crescent/gibbous, first/last quarter and the full/new moon. During the fight, [[Eyatlalli]] will imbue one of the sigils with her power; during non-special attacks, the player should stand on the sigil that is imbued, or they will take rapid damage; this initially starts at 1 damage per tick, but will quickly double up to 16 damage per tick while also applying a stack of the curse, which will rapidly kill players. The sigil will rotate clockwise after the Moon makes two standard attacks; upon hitting a full or new moon, the Moon will initiate a special attack. During a special attack, the player is generally allowed to stand anywhere in the arena.

===Standard attacks===
The Moon will face one of six potential directions based on the cycles above, where they will perform a unique melee attack that hits three times. The Moons have a ramping max hit based on how many of the attacks land in a row, so they can hit much harder than their combat level suggests. The first hit maxes 4, the second, 8, and the third, 20, for a total max of 32 damage in every series of hits. However, their attack has a unique rule in that if one of these hits miss, all hits succeeding it will also miss; for example, if the first hit in sequence does not land, the next two will also miss. 

Each standard attack in the 3-hit cycle applies 1, 2, and 5 stacks of the Curse of the Moons. The effects of the curse differs between the three bosses, but maxes out at 127 and slowly degrades by 2 every 5 [[ticks]]. Because of their typeless attacks and how the curse is applied, players are recommended to bring more defensive armour (especially for lower levels) to reduce overall damage. The Curse of the Moons debuff disappears fully after defeating a Moon of Peril.

Due to the timing of the standard attacks, weapon speed plays a larger role in determining DPS. For example, a 4-tick weapon can hit 3 times per cycle, whereas a 5-tick weapon can only hit twice. Because your character will take 1-2 ticks to run to the next glyph, you can exploit the attack cooldown mechanic to get in extra max hits. For example, it is possible to hit twice with a 4-tick weapon and then once with a 5-tick weapon in one cycle without losing any ticks. Similarly to common uses of the crystal halberd when there is forced downtime, weapons like a leaf-bladed battleaxe or a zombie axe may have a higher damage per hit, making them more effective as switches.

===Eclipse Moon===
'''The [[Eclipse Moon]] is weak to stab attacks''', and possesses 6 [[flat armour]], which reduces all [[hitsplat]]s dealt to her by 6; this is reduced to 4 during her Clone special attack.

Her Curse of the Moon will cause your attacks to occasionally be "glancing", stating {{Mes|Blinded by the Eclipse Moon's light, your attack glances off its shield!|colour=#ff8e32}}. Glancing attacks reduce your max hit by 12 (8 during the Clone phase); this is twice her flat armour. This occurs at a random chance scaling up to 100% at 100 stacks of the curse.

[[File:Eclipse Moon - Mimic attack.mp4|thumb|400px|A slow, high-hitting weapon attacks at a higher speed during the Eclipse Moon's Clone attack.]]
The boss will alternate between the following special attacks:
* ''New Moon'': '''Searing Rays''' - A moon shield will appear, and the Eclipse Moon will forcefully shove you behind it. She will begin attacking with rays of light, which can be avoided by moving alongside the moon shield. The shield will make one full rotation before the attack concludes. Getting hit deals minor damage, but it results in a large increase in the blinding effect.
** The shield moves at a walking pace and pauses on each corner of its route just long enough that a walking player can keep up with it. The timing is precise and may require occasional running if mistakes are made.
** An alternate running strategy is possible if you're familiar with the four corners of the pathway protected by the shield. Timing a run action from one corner of this pathway to the next, slightly after the shield begins moving, avoids all damage. 
* ''Full Moon'':  '''Clones''' - You are shoved to the centre of the room and are bound in place. Clones of the Eclipse Moon will spawn around you, attacking you in five cycles of three, for a total of 15 attacks. You must face your character toward each clone as it spawns to prevent damage. Doing so will parry the incoming attack, sending a melee attack with no delay back at the boss.
** Clicking to face your character towards the clone as soon as each appears is enough to perfectly parry the phase. You can click one tile away and this will still work.
** Accuracy is increased to 100% for each parry, so swapping to a slower and higher-hitting weapon is strongly recommended. Slash and Crush weapons also benefit from this increased accuracy.

===Blue Moon===
'''The [[Blue Moon]] is weak to crush attacks''', and possesses -5 [[flat armour]], which increases all [[hitsplat]]s dealt to her by 5. This makes multi-hitting weapons, such as [[Torag's hammers]], the [[dual macuahuitl]], the [[glacial temotli]] and the [[scythe of Vitur]] especially advantageous against her.

Her Curse of the Moon will cancel your next attack; this occurs once enough stacks of the curse have been accumulated:
* At 3 stacks, a message in the chatbox will state {{mes|The Blue Moon pierces your defence. The cold is starting to get in...|color=#00e6e6}}
* At 9 stacks, a message in the chatbox will state {{mes|The Blue Moon pierces your defence. Your joints are starting to lock up...|color=#00e6e6}}
* At 18 stacks, the Curse takes effect, with a message in the chatbox stating {{Mes|Your joints lock up as you go to attack. The cold is too much to bear!|color=#00e6e6}} After this, 18 stacks are removed from the Curse.

[[File:Blue Moon - Weapon Freeze attack.mp4|thumb|400px|Players can punch the block of ice twice before needing to move away.]]
The boss will alternate between the following special attacks:
* ''Full Moon'': '''Weapon Freeze''' - The Blue Moon will freeze the player's weapon out of their hands, placing them into one of three [[Frozen weapons|blocks of ice]]; the block the player should target is the one that glows with a blue hue. The player must break the block of ice via unarmed combat. During this time, the blocks will periodically plant shards of ice that will shatter shortly afterwards, dealing light damage if caught in the radius. The player is not able to equip other weapons until the block of ice is broken. Failing to break the block of ice will deal up to 28 damage to the player.
** The player can attack a block of ice twice before having to move to safety.
** If you are logged out or disconnect during this attack, the weapon will need to be reclaimed from Eyatlalli.
** A safespot exists one tile north from the centre of the ritual symbol.
** If using the Soulreaper axe when this attack starts you will lose all soul stacks and not regain any HP, possibly a bug.
** If there is no weapon equipped when this attack begins, the player will take 3-15 damage accompanied by a message stating {{mes|colour=#00e6e6|With no weapon in hand, your hands begin to freeze over!}}. Even though no weapons were frozen, the player still will need to destroy the [[Frozen weapons]] to avoid further damage.
* ''New Moon'': '''Frost Storm''' - Two braziers at opposing ends of the chamber are extinguished as freezing storms are conjured. The boss will heal herself five times during the storm, restoring 10 health for each unlit brazier up to a maximum of 100 hitpoints. To prevent this, run to the braziers and relight them whilst avoiding the moving storms that deal damage and force you to walk for two ticks. Control and click will ignore the forced walk to get across faster if you are hit by a tornado. Restoring both braziers will also remove a portion of stacks from Curse of the Moon. 
** There are safe spots on either side of the braziers, noted with footprints in the snow.
** You may choose to ignore the ''Frost Storm'' phase entirely, as long as you're dealing sufficient damage to make up for any healing the boss receives.
[[File:Blood Moon step under technique 16-9.mp4|thumb|width=400x400|The player steps under Blood Moon to avoid its third attack.]]
[[File:Blood Moon - dodging blood jaguars.mp4|thumb|400px|The player moves away right before the blood jaguar attacks.]]
===Blood Moon===
'''The [[Blood Moon]] is weak to slash attacks''', and possesses -2 [[flat armour]], which increases all [[hitsplat]]s dealt to her by 2. This makes multi-hitting weapons, such as the [[scythe of Vitur]] advantageous against her.

The [[Blood Moon]] is by far the most difficult of the Moons, possessing a unique passive effect that heals the boss whenever it or its mechanics damage the player. This forces the player to constantly out-damage the boss, and makes mechanical mistakes more punishing than they first appear.  

This pitting of the player's damage output against their own defence rolls can also make the difficulty and length of any particular fight wildly inconsistent, especially for lower-level players.

Lower-level players may wish to prioritise defence instead of attack with their gear to minimise the amount of health she regenerates from harming the player. Additionally, while the [[sulphur blades|sulphur blades']] multi-hit mechanic may seem a good match for the boss, the additional accuracy and slash defence that comes from pairing a one-handed weapon with a [[Dragon defender]] can significantly outweigh that benefit. 

====Standard attacks====
During the three standard attack hits, her Curse of the Moon will heal her for 1x the damage of her first hit and 2x her second. The multiplier of the third hit is erratic, but will heal her for 30-50 hitpoints regardless of the damage dealt. Successful hits are visually indicated by blobs of blood being sucked out of the player and into her.

It is possible to '''avoid the last hit and its heal''' by walking outside Eyatlalli's glyph during the attack. This maneuver requires concentration but will decrease your kill time significantly. To do this, look for a blood syphon coming out of you as Blood Moon's attack animation starts. If one appears, step under the boss for a tick, click back on the glyph and continue attacking.

====Special attacks====

The boss will alternate between the following special attacks:
* ''Full Moon'': '''Blood Rain''' - The Blood Moon will disappear and rain blood from above, forming temporary pools of blood throughout the room. Move off of the blood pools on the floor to avoid standing on them. Getting hit by a blood pool will deal up to 9 damage, and the Blood Moon will heal for 2x the damage dealt. Standing off the pools will deal minor chip damage to her.
** While Eyatlalli's glyph will reappear before this special attack is finished, any blood pools on the active moon symbol will still be dangerous.
* ''New Moon'': '''Blood Jaguar''' - Eight [[blood jaguar]]s will appear around the arena, with the Blood Moon dealing up to 15 damage onto the player in order to create them. Eyatlalli will have one of the eight moon symbols glow, indicating where the player must stand to avoid being hurt from the curse. The Blood Moon will also summon blood pools around her. The jaguars attack with a cleave-style melee attack on the two tiles in front of them, which can deal up to 9 damage, while the blood pools can deal up to 6 damage. The pools will despawn slightly before the jaguar attacks. Any damage incurred from these attacks will heal the Blood Moon for 3x and 2x the damage respectively. The Blood Moon will summon seven sets of blood pools before concluding the attack, while the jaguars will attack six times.
** Players must attack the jaguar to restore their lost health and can restore up to 25 health in this manner. As such, players must time their movement so that they can avoid the blood jaguar and the pools at once. A 4-tick weapon will allow the player to be in sync, so players using 5-tick weapons should be more cautious.

==Farming routes==
===General route===
# From the antechamber, head through the north-eastern entrance to the Streambound Cavern.
# Restore run energy as needed at the camp spot, and search the [[Supply crates (Neypotzli)|supply crates]] for anything you might need.
# Collect [[moonlight grub]]s to create 2-8 [[moonlight potion]]s. Use the potions to boost your melee stats and restore prayer between runs. Players with level 75 [[Hunter]] can also take a [[butterfly net]] to catch [[moonlight moths]] (or catch them barehanded with level 85 Hunter) to restore prayer in between bosses, if desired.
# Fish [[raw bream]] at the stream nearby and cook it. If your Hunter level is over 65 or is greater than your [[Fishing]] level, this can be skipped as moss lizards provide faster food than fishing.
# Enter the [[Eclipse Moon]] chamber to the south and fight the boss. After the fight, you will be teleported next to the camp spot in the Earthbound Cavern.
# Restore prayer (with potions or via catching moths), create additional moonlight potions and catch [[Moss Lizard|moss lizards]] as needed. With a high [[Cooking]] level, 1 [[raw moss lizard]] will provide 3 pieces of [[cooked moss lizard]]; as such, you can stock up on food by only cooking a handful of meats at a time and keeping the rest raw in your inventory, cooking more as needed in between bosses.
# Enter the [[Blue Moon]] chamber to the east and fight the boss. After the fight, you will be teleported next to the camp spot in the Ancient Prison.
# Enter the [[Blood Moon]] chamber to the east and fight the boss. After the fight, you will be teleported next to the camp spot in the Ancient Prison again.
# Head south to enter the Ancient Shrine to claim your loot. Head north to enter the Streambound Cavern.

Repeat steps 3-9 for as long as desired.

===Blood Moon Only===

Players wishing to efficiently farm only the Blood Moon boss can use the following route:

# Starting from the [[Lunar Chest]] after the first Blood Moon kill, return through the south door to the Ancient Prison.
# Run north to the cooking stove and restore run energy.
# Run east to the Blood Moon chamber and fight the boss. After defeating the boss, the player will be placed at the cooking stove in the Earthbound Cavern.
# Stock up on food and potions if needed, then run south-east through the cave entrance into the Streambound Cavern.
# Run directly south to the Lunar Chest room and claim your reward.

===Blue Moon Only===
Players wishing to efficiently farm only the Blue Moon boss can use the following route:

# Starting from the entrance to the Blue Moon boss, finish the kill and end up in the room with the Sulphur Naguas.
# Head south through the Sulphur Naguas.
# Loot the Lunar Chest.
# Head north through the passageway.
# Head north again through the passageway.
# Head north to the entrance to the Blue Moon.

===Eclipse Moon Only===
Players wishing to efficiently farm only the Eclipse Moon boss can use the following route:

# Starting from the entrance to the Eclipse Moon boss, finish the kill and end up at the cooking stove in the Earthbound Cavern.
# Head south-east and pass through the entrance to the Streambound Cavern.
# Run directly south to the Lunar Chest room and claim your reward.
# Head north through the passageway back to the Streambound Cavern, and stock up on food and potions if needed.
# Return back to the Eclipse Moon chamber.

==Equipment==
Each boss is weakest to a specific melee style and heavily resistant to magic and ranged attacks.

Due to the bosses' attack patterns, up to a certain point defence is a valuable stat for increasing DPS by reducing or eliminating the number of times a player must eat during the vulnerable phases. Defence additionally reduces the chance the Blood Moon will heal when attacking the player. Because of this, you should attempt to carefully balance strength boosting armour with armour that has high defensive stats. Avoid armour such as [[Obsidian armour|obsidian]], which has low defensive stats but a small strength bonus, in favour of tankier armour such as [[Barrows equipment]], which has high defensive stats but no strength bonus. Armour that features both high strength and high defence such as [[Bandos armour|Bandos]] is particularly effective.

While it is possible to kill all three moons with approximately 60 Defence with [[rune armour]] if using [[Steel Skin]], [[Ultimate Strength]], and [[Incredible Reflexes]], this is not particularly practical for repeat completions, and the Blood Moon in particular may be especially challenging. 

===Weapon choice===
Additionally, the Moons of Peril utilise a defensive stat known as [[flat armour]]. This mechanic directly increases or reduces the damage dealt of each hit by a flat amount. This leads to interesting interactions with weapons that hit multiple times; such as the [[scythe of Vitur]] performing worse than the [[Ghrazi rapier]] against Eclipse, or the [[dual macuahuitl]] beating out even the [[Inquisitor's mace]]. As a result of both this mechanic and the different weaknesses of each boss, it is recommended to bring a different weapon for each boss. Some exceptions include powerful weapons like the [[soulreaper axe]] or scythe of Vitur which can comfortably kill each without a necessary swap. For a cheaper alternative the [[Zamorakian hasta]] is more than adequate for all three bosses if switching attack styles.

Defence-reducing [[special attacks]] and [[Death Charge]] have no effect on the Moons of Peril.

===Other items===
Hunter, Fishing and Herblore supply crates provide an infinite number of [[Vial of water|vials of water]], [[pestle and mortar]]s, [[big fishing net]]s, [[rope]] and [[butterfly net]]s to allow collecting and crafting all dungeon resources.

[[Moonlight potion]]s fulfil the role of prayer restoration and combat stat boosts for the boss. Since the moonlight potion's boosts scale with [[Herblore]] level, you may want to bring 1 [[super defence]] or [[super combat potion]] if your Herblore level is less than 66. 

[[Cooked bream]] and [[cooked moss lizard]] serve as easy to obtain and powerful food supplies in the dungeon. Cooked bream scales with [[Cooking]] and [[Fishing]] levels, while cooked moss lizard scales with Cooking and [[Hunter]] levels. You may want to bring alternate foods if your associated levels are below 50.

