*A [[soulreaper axe]] or other slow, high hitting weapon such as an [[elder maul]], [[colossal blade]], or [[godsword]], is used on the Eclipse Moon during the Clone attack.
** [[Dharok's set]], alongside either a [[dwarven rock cake]] or [[locator orb]], can be used to quickly kill off the Eclipse Moon instead, but requires close monitoring of the player's health.
*[[Dragon claws]], or other special attack weapon.
*Any additional weapon switches to match boss weaknesses.
* Supplies: 
** Food: [[rope]] for catching lizards or [[big fishing net]] for catching fish if your Hunter is low. At high cooking, 1 raw moss lizard will yield 3 cooked moss lizards. Cooking raw moss lizards as needed can save inventory space. All available inside the dungeon.
**Prayer: [[pestle and mortar]] for making [[Moonlight potion|moonlight potions]], more doses received with higher herblore. Alternatively also a [[butterfly net]] for catching [[Moonlight moth|moonlight moths]] to restore prayer if your Herblore is lower.
*[[Moonlight potion|Moonlight potions]], which act as a super combat and prayer potion in one.
*Food in the form of [[cooked bream]] or [[cooked moss lizard]]. All made inside the dungeon.
*An emergency teleport. (Optional, all the fights have quick escapes)
*An optional [[Book of the Dead]] and [[rune pouch]] with runes for [[Thrall|Thralls]].

